  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set name = \"python-suitesparse-graphblas\" %}\n{% set version = \"10.5.0.0\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: {{ name|lower }}\n  version: {{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/source/s/suitesparse_graphblas/suitesparse_graphblas-{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 66aec95b05bc6ebb2c85d4f41ff906ec954db51d95158e1b168056dfd475d683\n\nbuild:\n  skip: true  # [py<311]\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    # The sdist ships a utils.c that was cythonized against numpy 2.5 and only compiles\n    # with numpy >=2.5 headers; drop it so it is regenerated for the numpy used here.\n    - {{ PYTHON }} -c \"import pathlib; pathlib.Path('suitesparse_graphblas/utils.c').unlink(missing_ok=True)\"\n    - {{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - python                                 # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cross-python_{{ target_platform }}     # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cython                                 # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - numpy                                  # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - cffi                                   # [build_platform != target_platform]\n    - {{ compiler(\"c\") }}\n    - {{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=77\n    - setuptools-git-versioning\n    - cffi\n    - cython\n    - graphblas ={{ version.rsplit('.', 1)[0] }}\n    - numpy\n  run:\n    - python\n    - cffi\n    - numpy >=1.24\n\ntest:\n  imports:\n    - suitesparse_graphblas\n  commands:\n    - pip check\n    - python -c \"import platform ; print(platform.machine())\"\n    - python -c \"from suitesparse_graphblas import lib, ffi\"\n    # Fail loudly if libgraphblas was built without OpenMP. GraphBLAS only\n    # warns at configure time and still builds a serial library, so this is\n    # otherwise invisible: graphblas 10.5.0 shipped that way on osx-arm64\n    # while still depending on llvm-openmp.\n    - python -c \"import suitesparse_graphblas as s; from suitesparse_graphblas import lib, ffi; s.initialize(); p = ffi.new('int32_t*'); assert lib.GrB_Global_get_INT32(lib.GrB_GLOBAL, p, lib.GxB_LIBRARY_OPENMP) == lib.GrB_SUCCESS; assert p[0], 'libgraphblas was built without OpenMP'\"\n    - pytest -v --pyargs suitesparse_graphblas\n  requires:\n    - pip\n    - pytest\n\nabout:\n  home: https://github.com/GraphBLAS/python-suitesparse-graphblas\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_family: Apache\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Python CFFI binding around SuiteSparse::GraphBLAS\n  description: |\n    Python CFFI binding around SuiteSparse::GraphBLAS. This is a base package that exposes\n    only the low level CFFI API bindings and symbols. This package is shared by the syntax\n    bindings pygraphblas and python-graphblas.\n  dev_url: https://github.com/GraphBLAS/python-suitesparse-graphblas\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - jim22k\n    - eriknw\n    - michelp\n",
